      "description": {
        "fun": "The flame on Charmander's tail has burned since it hatched, and it shows how Charmander feels: bright when it's healthy, weak when it's tired, wavering when it's happy and blazing when it's angry. It's said Charmander would die if the flame went out, though a healthy one just steams in the rain. Its name blends 'char' and 'salamander', the lizard of folklore said to live in fire.",
        "guide": "A small orange lizard Pokémon with a flame that has burned at the tip of its tail since birth. The flame shows its health and mood, and it is said Charmander would die if it went out. It is one of the first partner Pokémon of Kanto and evolves into Charmeleon.",
        "tagline": "A little lizard whose tail flame shows exactly how it feels",
        "sources": [
